For every integer $J\ge0$, there is a constant $D_J$, depending only on the fixed root data and $J$, such that for all $v,x,\phi$ and $0\le j\le J$, $$\label{geom:ext-bound}
 \sum_{\psi\in\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}(A_v,k^\times)}
 \dim_k\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}^j_{\mathcal X}
       (j_{v,!}L_{v,\psi},j_{x,!}E_{x,\phi})\le D_J.$$

outputs.exact_statement:
For every integer $J\ge0$, there is a constant $D_J$, depending only on the fixed root data and $J$, such that for all $v,x,\phi$ and $0\le j\le J$, $$\label{geom:ext-bound}
 \sum_{\psi\in\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}(A_v,k^\times)}
 \dim_k\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}^j_{\mathcal X}
       (j_{v,!}L_{v,\psi},j_{x,!}E_{x,\phi})\le D_J.$$ The same bound holds, after increasing the constant if necessary, in invariant open unions containing the relevant strata. Bounded shifts of the two arguments are allowed by increasing $J$.

The modules $P_{x,\phi}$ are projective. Let $\widehat A_x$ be the ordinary linear characters of $A_x$, with $\xi\mapsto\bar\xi$ their modular reductions, and set $$\label{geom:torus-sum}
 \Psi_{x,\phi}=(-1)^{\ell(x)}
       \sum_{\substack{\xi\in\widehat A_x\\\bar\xi=\phi}}
              R_{T_x}^{\mathbf G}(\xi).$$ If $n_{x,\phi;y,\eta}$ are the multiplicities in the specified standard flag, the ordinary lift character of $P_{x,\phi}$ is $$\label{geom:projective-character}
 \chi_{P_{x,\phi}}=
       \sum_{y,\eta} n_{x,\phi;y,\eta}\Psi_{y,\eta},
 \qquad \sum_{y,\eta}n_{x,\phi;y,\eta}\le L.$$ These projective characters and the $\Psi_{x,\phi}$ have the same linear span in characteristic zero, and that span contains the regular character of $\Gamma$.

The stabilizer quotient $W_\rho=N_G(\mathbf L,\rho)/L$ is the relative rational Weyl group of $\mathbf C_L$ in $\mathbf C$. On a packet outside the even-sign case its factor is $\prod_b W(B_{r_{i,b}})$. On an even-sign packet it is $$\label{end:total-parity}
 \left\{(w_b)_b\in\prod_b W(B_{r_{i,b}}):
          \sum_b \operatorname{flip}(w_b)=0\pmod2\right\},$$ where $\operatorname{flip}$ is the parity of the number of changed coordinate signs. Different choices of the size multiplicities $r_{i,b}$ give nonconjugate cuspidal pairs.

For one even-sign packet with at least one chunk, the simple modules of its endomorphism algebra are indexed by the following rule. For every size $b$ choose an ordered pair of $e_b$-regular partitions of total size $r_{i,b}$, where $$\label{end:quantum-e}
 e_b=\begin{cases}
 d_i,&b=1\text{ and }d_i>1,\\
 p,&\text{otherwise}.
 \end{cases}$$ Identify these choices under simultaneous exchange of the two components for all sizes. Each nonfixed orbit contributes one simple, and each fixed choice contributes two. If there are no chunks, there is one simple.
